{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013DCs1VaCvBEjVjpaSoA68A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n**`cmd/timeout/main.go`** — Implements R1.1-R1.4:\n- **R1.1**: Runs COMMAND with ARGS, kills with SIGTERM via process group (`syscall.Kill(-pgid, SIGTERM)`) if duration exceeded\n- **R1.2**: Supports fractional durations (e.g., `0.5`, `0.01`) via `strconv.ParseFloat`\n- **R1.3**: Supports suffix multipliers `s`, `m`, `h`, `d` with seconds as default\n- **R1.4**: Duration 0 imposes no time limit (timer simply not started)\n- Proper exit codes: 0 on success, 124 on timeout, 128+signum for signals, 125/126/127 for errors\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n\n**`cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go`** — 12 differential tests against `gtimeout`:\n- Command completes/fails before timeout, command exceeds timeout, fractional duration, suffix seconds/minutes, duration zero (with and without suffix), error cases (no args, missing command, command not found, invalid duration)\n- Skips gracefully if `gtimeout` is not installed\n- Uses `clearStderr` normalizer on error cases where stderr messages naturally differ between implementations\n\nAll 12 tests pass, `go build` and `go vet` clean."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2450,"cache_read_input_tokens":34151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2450},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90c15c96-339f-482a-9f6f-05c431a9e14f","uuid":"57530278-36f0-47aa-940d-e0b82b4149e1"}
